    "body": "Recently, I found out that Element Web doesn't store the history encrypted. On MacOS this results in complete chat history being stored in ˜/Library/Application Support/Element/IndexedDB/vector_vector_0.indexeddb.blob, which is a huge privacy problem.\r\n\r\nI think it would contribute greatly to user's privacy when the indexed DB would be protected with a passphrase, for which the  user gets a prompt after first login and sets a cookie that expires in a set amount of time.\r\n\r\nAnother approach would be to allow the user to choose not to store history to disk / to store it only in an in-memory database.",
